From 537a298829c9d0820061d5d7479662876e105aff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Lukschander <oliver.lukschander@golf.at>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:58:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm: apple: iomfb: log crtc active/mode state for a stuck 0x0
 tunnel commit

DP tunnel connect now reaches DPRX_DONE=1 and 4 lanes on the first
attempt (0136/0137/0138), and a genuine reconnect now works after a
physical replug (0138), but there is still no picture: Hyprland shows the
tunnel connector ("BNQ BenQ LCD T4M01233019", correct EDID) stuck
applying a 0x0 mode.

A research pass into dcp_hotplug()'s existing !dcp_is_usb4_output(dcp)
retrain-nudge exclusion found: (1) the exclusion's own history traces to
an unrelated, since-deleted debug shim, not a documented hazard with the
retrain path itself; but (2) removing it would very likely be a no-op
regardless, traced through actual DRM atomic-commit semantics --
drm_atomic_helper_reset_crtc() never touches crtc_state->mode, so
replaying an already-active CRTC's state just re-triggers the same
degenerate 0x0 commit dcp_crtc_atomic_modeset() already silently
swallows; and (3) narrowing the gate would also reintroduce
DRM_MODE_LINK_STATUS_BAD marking, which per that same exclusion's own
commit message has direct precedent for making Hyprland refuse to commit
a mode at all. No gate change proposed.

Add two additive dev_info() diagnostics instead, no control-flow change:
in dcp_crtc_atomic_modeset()'s existing 0x0 bail-out, log crtc_state->active
and dcp_is_usb4_output(); in dcp_hotplug(), log the connector's bound
crtc/active/mode unconditionally (not gated on usb4). Together these
settle, on the next capture, whether a real-but-degenerate atomic commit
is landing for this connector (active=1, 0x0 mode) versus no commit ever
reaching it at all -- before spending a hardware reboot on a fix that
might target the wrong layer entirely.

Built and verified (make in src/appledrm/, vermagic
7.1.12-2.5-1-ARCH, no new warnings; only iomfb.o recompiled).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb.c
index c2745c192..c447441f6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/apple/iomfb.c
@@ -283,6 +283,23 @@ void dcp_hotplug(struct work_struct *work)
 	dev_info(dcp->dev, "%s() connected:%d valid_mode:%d nr_modes:%u\n", __func__,
 		 connector->connected, dcp->valid_mode, dcp->nr_modes);
 
+	/*
+	 * Diagnostic (candidate 0139): report whether this connector has an
+	 * active CRTC bound and what mode it already holds, unconditionally
+	 * (not gated on dcp_is_usb4_output), so a next capture can tell
+	 * whether Hyprland ever actually committed anything for a
+	 * USB4-tunneled connector versus never touching it at all.
+	 */
+	{
+		struct drm_crtc *crtc = connector->base.state ?
+					 connector->base.state->crtc : NULL;
+		dev_info(dcp->dev,
+			 "%s: crtc=%p active=%d mode=%dx%d\n", __func__,
+			 crtc, crtc && crtc->state ? crtc->state->active : -1,
+			 crtc && crtc->state ? crtc->state->mode.hdisplay : -1,
+			 crtc && crtc->state ? crtc->state->mode.vdisplay : -1);
+	}
+
 	if (!connector->connected) {
 		drm_edid_free(connector->drm_edid);
 		connector->drm_edid = NULL;
@@ -516,8 +533,21 @@ int dcp_crtc_atomic_modeset(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 		return 0;
 
 	/* ignore no mode, poweroff is handled elsewhere */
-	if (crtc_state->mode.hdisplay == 0 && crtc_state->mode.vdisplay == 0)
+	if (crtc_state->mode.hdisplay == 0 && crtc_state->mode.vdisplay == 0) {
+		/*
+		 * Diagnostic (candidate 0139, see notes/2026-09-24-0139-*.md):
+		 * a USB4-tunneled connector has been observed stuck applying
+		 * a 0x0 mode with no picture. This silent bail-out is the
+		 * only place that would ever run for such a commit -- log
+		 * whether it's actually reached, and whether the CRTC is
+		 * active, to tell a real-but-degenerate atomic commit apart
+		 * from no commit ever landing at all.
+		 */
+		dev_info(dcp->dev,
+			 "%s: 0x0 commit for crtc active=%d (usb4=%d)\n",
+			 __func__, crtc_state->active, dcp_is_usb4_output(dcp));
 		return 0;
+	}
 
 	switch (dcp->fw_compat) {
 	case DCP_FIRMWARE_V_12_3:
-- 
2.55.0

